case ptab-ipr-defense
uses ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board ^0.1.0, cafc ^0.1.0
as_of 2026-08-26
summary "IPR defense by a patent owner at the PTAB (35 U.S.C. §§311-319), from the Patent Owner Preliminary Response through a final written decision, with appeal to the CAFC."
notes "Protagonist is the PATENT OWNER defending against a petitioner's inter partes review, not the petitioner. Uses `ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board` + `cafc` (links.json's `cafc@ptab` instance supplies the appeal, remanding only back to the Board). The events replay to the notice of filing date accorded (the POPR clock start), leaving the matter at the § 315(b) time-bar fact, which its guards derive from the service and filing dates into `popr-window`, so the graph begins where the patent owner's own defense choices begin, skipping the pre-suit/petition-filing steps that are the petitioner's decisions, not the defense's. JUDGMENT CALL (perspective mapping): this pack's actor vocabulary (schemaVersion 2 as of a later migration, but `roles` is still just the default identity mapping — petitioner→self, patent-owner→self, board→nature; the pack distinguishes petitioner and patent-owner actors) uses `petitioner` for the PETITIONER's moves (files the petition, moves for joinder, replies, opposes amendment — verified against every `actor: petitioner` edge in the pack) and buckets the patent owner's own moves (file/waive POPR, file/skip response, settle, move to amend, waive oral argument, request rehearing/Director review, decide whether to appeal) with patent-owner moves now explicitly assigned to `patent-owner` and neutral steps assigned to `either`. `perspective` below assigns `patent-owner` to self and `petitioner` to opponent, exposing the patent owner's defense choices and the petitioning adversary, leaving `examiner`/`office` at their default `nature` (the Board and the Federal Circuit acting adjudicatively). This is the closest reading the CURRENT pack data supports without editing pack content (out of this scenario's scope); it necessarily also treats some genuinely joint/neutral `either` edges as 'our' choice — flagged here rather than silently assumed. The pack now gives the patent owner a dedicated `patent-owner` actor. SECOND JUDGMENT CALL (payoffs): several CAFC-side and post-FWD PTAB terminals (`appeal-forfeited-unappealed`, `cafc@ptab::window-blown-ptab`/`dismissed-failure-to-prosecute`/`rule36-affirmance`/`affirmed`/`dismissed-jurisdictional-defect`/`cert-not-sought`/`cert-denied`/`cert-granted`) are reachable regardless of which prior FWD outcome preceded them — a known engine/pack-content limitation (docs/CRITIQUE.md, 'Markov on the node': the graph has no memory of which FWD led here). Rather than inventing false precision, this scenario assigns those a flat mid-range illustrative value ($1,500,000, half of the $3,000,000 illustrative patent value used for a clean win) and says so per-terminal below instead of leaving it unstated. All dollar figures assume an illustrative $3,000,000 patent value (this patent's licensing/enforcement value if it survives intact) and a $700/hr blended rate; neither is sourced (no real matter identified) — override both per actual matter."

source "35 U.S.C. §319 — appeal of a PTAB final written decision to the Federal Circuit" {
  url "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/35/319"
}

source "35 U.S.C. §315(e) — IPR estoppel attaching at final written decision" {
  url "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/35/315"
}

perspective { patent-owner: self, petitioner: opponent }

parties {
  owner: patent-owner Corporation
  petitioning-party: petitioner Corporation
}

// Complaint served 2025-09-15, petition filed 2026-06-01: inside the
// 35 U.S.C. § 315(b) one-year bar, which the time-bar check's guards
// derive from these events, so no `facts` entry states it.
events {
  patent-granted-1: 2021-03-02 PatentGranted() on owner
  complaint-served-1: 2025-09-15 ComplaintServed() on petitioning-party
  ipr-petition-filed-1: 2026-06-01 IprPetitionFiled() by petitioning-party
  filing-date-noticed-1: 2026-06-18 FilingDateNoticed() on owner
}

// The Federal Circuit remands a PTAB decision to the Board: the remand
// destination is a matter fact (lit/cafc's `remand-destination`).
facts { cafc::remand-destination: cafc::remand-route-ptab }

stakes {
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::ipr-time-barred: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::claims-disclaimed-preinstitution: 1_500_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::institution-denied-merits: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::institution-denied-fintiv: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::ipr-terminated-settlement: 2_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::adverse-judgment-terminal: 0.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::fwd-all-unpatentable: 0.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::fwd-all-confirmed: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::fwd-mixed: 1_500_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::appeal-forfeited-unappealed: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::window-blown-ptab: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::settled-in-mediation: 2_000_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::dismissed-failure-to-prosecute: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::rule36-affirmance: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::affirmed: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::reversed: 3_000_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::affirmed-in-part-reversed-in-part: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::dismissed-jurisdictional-defect: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::remanded-to-ptab: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::cert-not-sought: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::cert-denied: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::cert-granted: 1_500_000.usd
}

analysis { params: { rate: 700.usd / 1.hours, opp_rate: 650.usd / 1.hours } }
